{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Perhaps I will be able.</b> After you curse him." "<b>We will strike him.</b> I by warfare, and you by curse." "<b>Whom you bless is blessed.</b> His power was not to bless, but to curse — by calling sin to mind or by aiming at the appointed hour, as our Sages of blessed memory said regarding blessing (Berakhot 7a). Therefore Balak did not ask him to bless him for victory, or that he be able to take a stand against him, but said, 'I know that whom you bless is blessed' — for Balaam's own honor, to indicate that he did not consider him merely one who harms."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:39.190006162Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}